;;;
;;; THE STATEMENTS.  "f_n -> f in the topology of H(U)" is UNIF-ON-COMPACTA(u, s, f) with
;;; s in FUN(NN, CC-HOL-FNS(u)) and f in FUN(u, CC) (f is then holomorphic: Prop 3.44,
;;; holomorphic-limit-on-compacta; the user's decision of 2026-10-14 keeps the sequential form).
;;; "f is constant" is: some c in CC with f(z) = c for every z in u.  "Bounded" is CC-HOL-BOUNDED of
;;; the image, as in cc-montel.  "Converges pointwise to g" is, for every z in u, CONVERGES-TO(CC-MS,
;;; k |-> s_k(z), g(z)).  Injective on u is written out (z, w in u, f(z) = f(w) => z = w).
;;; Remark 5.24's "for infinitely many n" is stated contrapositively, as the notes' last sentence of
;;; the remark: if f is not constant and f(c) = a, then for every r > 0 and all large k, f_k takes the
;;; value a in B(c, r); this local form is what 5.25 uses.
;;;
;;; THE ROUTES AGAINST THE NOTES.
;;; * 5.19: as the notes, through the subsequence principle of the Frechet METRIC of C(u)
;;;   (subsequence-principle, frm-converges-iff, cc-fr-conv-iff-unif-on-compacta): every subsequence
;;;   has, by Montel (cc-montel), a further subsequence converging on compacta, whose limit is g.
;;; * 5.23 / 5.24: the notes use Corollary 4.21 (the zero-counting integral), which the tree does
;;;   not have.  The elementary route of the brief instead: if f(c) = a and f is not constant, the
;;;   zeros of f - a do not accumulate at c (2.12, holomorphic-identity-principle), so f /= a on a
;;;   punctured disc B(c, 2 rho); |f - a| >= m > 0 on the circle of radius rho, since 1/(f - a) is
;;;   holomorphic, hence continuous, on the punctured disc and so bounded on the compact circle
;;;   (cc-exhaust-exhaustive, cc-continuous-bounded-on-exhaust); for large k, |f_k - f| <= m/4 on the
;;;   circle and at c; if f_k /= a on the disc, the mean value inequality for 1/(f_k - a)
;;;   (holomorphic-mean-value-bound) gives |f_k(c) - a| >= 3m/4, against |f_k(c) - a| <= m/4.
;;; * 5.25: as the notes, from the local form of 5.24 at two points z /= w with f(z) = f(w), on the
;;;   disjoint discs of radius |z - w|/2.
;;; * 5.20: the module laws of CA-5's cc-fn-module-is-module are stated for C(u) only; (14)-(16)
;;;   prove them once for any closed class v, so H(u) is an instance.  Linearity is CA-5's
;;;   cc-deriv-linear; continuity is CA-5's cc-deriv-continuous-on-hol (in C(u)) carried to H(u)
;;;   by (16).  IS-CONT-LIN is the tree's sequential continuity for a seminorm family.
;;;
